{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.Zeta8WitnessLevel2Su2","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.Zeta8WitnessLevel2Su2","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.RootsOfUnity.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Cyclotomic.Basic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.wenzlAnnihilatorHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.wenzlAnnihilatorHolds","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/zeta8-witness-level2-su2.lean#L161-L174","doc":"**Wenzl-annihilator target at `q = ζ` (level-2 SU(2) Verlinde truncation)**,\nas a **predicate** on the character value: the Hecke character `χ^λ` at\n`q = ζ` (given as a function of the first-column length) vanishes for every\npartition `λ` with first-column length `≥ 4` — the categorical content of the\nuniversal `Φ_8` cancellation at `M = 7`.\n\nNamed (§3b), not asserted: the previous\n`wenzl_annihilator (_n) (firstCol) (_h : 4 ≤ firstCol) :\n∃ chi, chi = 0 := ⟨0, rfl⟩` was trivially true in every ring and used none of\nits hypotheses. A full proof needs the Wenzl projector machinery not yet in\nMathlib. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.qInt_four_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.qInt_four_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/zeta8-witness-level2-su2.lean#L128-L159","doc":"**Identity (3): `[4]_q = 0` at `q = ζ`** (first vanishing quantum\ninteger).\n\nSince `ζ^4` is a primitive 2nd root of unity, `ζ^4 = −1 = ζ^(−4)`,\nconsequently the numerator `q^4 - q^(-4)` vanishes while the denominator is\nnonzero. The vanishing `[4]_q = 0` is the Wenzl projector boundary\nfor the level-`k = 2` SU(2) Verlinde truncation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:zeta8-witness-level2-su2","label":"prop:zeta8-witness-level2-su2","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/zeta8-witness-level2-su2.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.qInt_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.qInt_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/zeta8-witness-level2-su2.lean#L112-L126","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical singular-locus-guarded bracket.**\n\nThe guard here is written `q = q⁻¹`, which is the same locus as\n`q − q⁻¹ = 0` (`sub_eq_zero`) — so this is the two-sided `qIntBalClSing`, not\nthe one-sided `qIntBalCl`.  That matters in this file specifically: the roots of\nunity it works with sit exactly where the balanced denominator degenerates, so\nwhich guard is in force is not a formality here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.qInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.qInt","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/zeta8-witness-level2-su2.lean#L108-L110","doc":"The quantum integer `[n]_q = (q^n − q^(−n)) / (q − q^(−1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.hecke_eigenvalues","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.hecke_eigenvalues","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/zeta8-witness-level2-su2.lean#L99-L106","doc":"The Hecke quadratic relation eigenvalue split over a field (an\nintegral domain): if `(σ − ζ)(σ + ζ⁻¹) = 0` then `σ = ζ` or\n`σ = −ζ⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.zeta_pow_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.zeta_pow_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/zeta8-witness-level2-su2.lean#L89-L97","doc":"**Identity (2): `σ_i` has order 8 at `q = ζ`**.\n\nDirect consequence of primitivity: `ζ^k ≠ 1` for `0 < k < 8`. The\nHecke eigenvalues `ζ` and `−ζ⁻¹ = ζ³` both have order 8, so\n`ord(σ_i) = lcm(8, 8) = 8`, matching the empirical\n`M_first_Φ_8 = 7 = ord − 1` boundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.qPoch_seven_eq_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.qPoch_seven_eq_eight","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/zeta8-witness-level2-su2.lean#L57-L87","doc":"**Identity (1): `(ζ; ζ)_7 = 8`**.\n\nThe q-Pochhammer at a primitive 8th root of unity, truncated at\n`m = 7 = ord(ζ) − 1`, evaluates to the integer `8 = ord(ζ)`.\n\nAlgebraic derivation: from `X^8 − 1 = ∏_{k=0}^{7}(X − ζ^k)`,\ndividing by `(X − 1)` gives `X^7 + ⋯ + 1 = ∏_{k=1}^{7}(X − ζ^k)`.\nEvaluating at `X = 1`: LHS = `8`, RHS = `∏_{k=1}^{7}(1 − ζ^k) = (ζ; ζ)_7`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.qPoch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Zeta8Witness.qPoch","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/zeta8-witness-level2-su2.lean#L52-L55","doc":"The q-Pochhammer symbol `(q; q)_m = Π_{k=1..m} (1 − q^k)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}